--- PARITY MAP (web -> native) ---
useMotionPreference (reduce)            -> IMotionPreferenceSource (P1/S8 seam, reused from AIThinkingIndicator):
                                           SystemMotionPreferenceSource over Components.Motion.MotionPreference (prod, read-once),
                                           StaticMotionPreferenceSource / FakeMotionSource (tests)
sizeMap sm/md/lg (px + stroke)          -> SpinnerRegistration.Resolve(SpinnerSize) -> SpinnerMetrics(24/22, 48/14, 80/10)
svg path d="M112 30L62 108h34L78 170l58-82h-34z" (viewBox 200)
                                        -> SpinnerRegistration.BoltVertices (6 absolute points) -> closed filled PathGeometry;
                                           BoltPathLength = measured closed perimeter (~384.5) drives the stroke-dash draw
@keyframes boltDraw (2s ease-in-out)    -> SpinnerRegistration.DrawKeyframes -> looping Storyboard: StrokeDashOffset (draw),
                                           white Fill opacity (fill-in), bolt-canvas Opacity (fade) per frame
.spinner-bolt-glow (cyan #22d3ee + emerald #10b981 drop-shadow)
                                        -> two thicker colour-tinted stroke copies behind the white bolt (native halo stand-in;
                                           the platform animation idiom here is XAML Storyboards, not Composition blur)
fillOpacity / strokeDasharray / strokeDashoffset (reduce ? ...)
                                        -> SpinnerProjection.FillOpacity / StrokeDashed / InitialDashProgress
label (optional caption)                -> SpinnerProjection.HasLabel / Label (TextBlock, text-sm, TextSecondary token)
aria-label={label ?? 'Loading'}         -> SpinnerProjection.AccessibleName (caller label, else i18n default)
'Loading' default literal               -> translation.global.loading (web i18n: global.loading = "Loading") via ILocalizer
role="status"                           -> LiveRegion.Configure (polite) + AutomationProperties.Name + FrameworkElementAutomationPeer (Image)
component mount                         -> SpinnerDiagnostics.RecordViewOpened() => "view.opened slug=Spinner" (once, P1/S11)

--- STATES (web source is a pure presentational loading mark — no query, no async data) ---
full motion  -> bolt draws itself (dash sweep), fills, holds, fades, redraws; 2s loop   [reproduced + tested]
reduced motion -> static solid filled bolt, no draw cycle (web prefers-reduced-motion)  [reproduced + tested]
with caption -> caption shown beneath bolt + it is the accessible name                  [reproduced + tested]
no caption   -> caption hidden; accessible name falls back to i18n "Loading"            [reproduced + tested]
sizes sm/md/lg -> 24/48/80 px boxes, 22/14/10 strokes                                    [reproduced + tested]
loading / empty / error / stale / offline : DO NOT EXIST in the web source (the spinner IS the loading state; it reads no
network data) — not stubbed, not invented; documented like the sibling AnimatedNumber/VisuallyHidden dataless surfaces.

